# `shadow/generated.mbt` is tracked. It was generated at build time once, and
# `moon publish` is what killed that: the packaged zip is re-checked in a
# scratch directory with no `.git`, where the generator does not answer — it
# spins — so the check never returned and nothing could be published. The
# packager only ships tracked files, so a build-time artifact would have been
# missing from the zip regardless.
#
# It no longer carries any checkout's git state (see the file itself), so the
# `git diff --exit-code` in scripts/ci.sh stays green across checkouts, and
# `scripts/shadow.sh` refreshes it by hand when `moon.mod` changes.
